      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the values of \\(A\\), \\(B\\), \\(C\\), and \\(D\\) that satisfy the given conditions and then calculate the product \\(A \\times B \\times C \\times D\\).\n\nLet's start by defining the conditions:\n1. \\(A + 2 = B - 2 = C \\times 2 = D \\div 2\\)\n2. \\(A + B + C + D = 36\\)\n\nFrom the first condition, we can express \\(A\\), \\(B\\), \\(C\\), and \\(D\\) in terms of a common variable \\(k\\):\n\\[A = k - 2\\]\n\\[B = k + 2\\]\n\\[C = \\frac{k}{2}\\]\n\\[D = 2k\\]\n\nNow, we substitute these into the second equation:\n\\[\n(k - 2) + (k + 2) + \\frac{k}{2} + 2k = 36\n\\]\nSimplifying the left side, we get:\n\\[\nk - 2 + k + 2 + \\frac{k}{2} + 2k = 36\n\\]\nCombining like terms, we obtain:\n\\[\n4k + \\frac{k}{2} = 36\n\\]\nTo eliminate the fraction, we can multiply the entire equation by 2:\n\\[\n8k + k = 72\n\\]\n\\[\n9k = 72\n\\]\nSolving for \\(k\\), we get:\n\\[\nk = 8\n\\]\n\nNow we can find the values of \\(A\\), \\(B\\), \\(C\\), and \\(D\\):\n\\[\nA = 8 - 2 = 6\n\\]\n\\[\nB = 8 + 2 = 10\n\\]\n\\[\nC = \\frac{8}{2} = 4\n\\]\n\\[\nD = 2 \\times 8 = 16\n\\]\n\nFinally, we calculate the product \\(A \\times B \\times C \\times D\\):\n\\[\nA \\times B \\times C \\times D = 6 \\times 10 \\times 4 \\times 16\n\\]\n\nWe can compute this product step by step:\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60\n\\]\n\\[\n60 \\times 4 = 240\n\\]\n\\[\n240 \\times 16 = 3840\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of the product \\(A \\times B \\times C \\times D\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3840}\n\\]",
